---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Plain-language and short on purpose. NOT reviewed by a lawyer — see the notice
 * at the foot of the page, and remove it once it has been.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro'
import { site } from '../lib/site.ts'

const updated = 'September 2026'
---

<Public title="Privacy" description="What FleetView Compliance collects, and what it does not do with it.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-ink-700">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The short version</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          We collect what we need to track your deadlines and run your account. We do not sell it,
          we do not share it with brokers, insurers or load boards, and we do not use your
          operational data to build products for anyone else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What we hold</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          <li><strong>Account information</strong> — names, email addresses and phone numbers of the people who sign in.</li>
          <li><strong>Carrier information</strong> — your USDOT number and what the public federal record says about your business.</li>
          <li><strong>Driver and vehicle records</strong> — including documents you upload, such as medical certificates and licences. This is sensitive personal information about your employees, and we treat it that way.</li>
          <li><strong>Operational records</strong> — loads, trips and the documents attached to them.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage logs</strong> — enough to keep the service running and secure.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Where it comes from</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          From you, and from public federal and California government records that anyone can
          look up. We re-check the public record periodically so we can tell you when something
          changes on it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who else sees it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Only the service providers we need to operate: hosting and database, file storage, and
          the services that send our email and text messages. They process data on our
          instructions and for no other purpose. We disclose data otherwise only if the law
          requires it — and if that happens and we are permitted to tell you, we will.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          If you generate a proof link and send it to a broker or an underwriter, you are sharing
          it — that is the point of the feature — and it is your decision who receives it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your drivers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Drivers do not have accounts here. Where we send a driver a link to supply a document,
          that link is single-purpose and expires. Some records — such as a return-to-duty
          follow-up testing schedule — are restricted by federal rule from being shown to the
          driver, and our system enforces that.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Keeping and deleting</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Compliance records have legally required retention periods — a driver qualification file,
          for instance, must be kept for as long as the driver is employed and three years after.
          We keep records for at least as long as the rule that produced them requires. You can
          export everything at any time, and on request we will delete what we are not required
          to retain.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">California rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          If you are a California resident you have rights to know what we hold about you, to
          correct it, to delete it, and not to be discriminated against for exercising them. We do
          not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined under California law.
          Write to us to exercise any of this.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          {site.email ? site.email : 'Contact details are on the About page.'}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
      <strong>Draft.</strong> This policy has not yet been reviewed by a lawyer, and the operating
      entity is not yet named. Both must be done before launch.
    </p>
  </section>
</Public>
